    "base_en": "Indian gluten-free breakfast",
    "ingredients_en": "220 g tapioca pearls, 250 g potatoes, 70 g roasted peanuts, 25 ml neutral oil, 1 tsp cumin seeds, 1 small green chilli, 1/2 tsp sugar, 1 lime, 15 g coriander, 3/4 tsp salt",
    "recipe_en": "<p>Rinse the tapioca, cover with just enough water and soak for 4 hours, then drain well</p><p>Boil the potatoes until almost tender and cut into small cubes</p><p>Mix the tapioca with the ground peanuts, sugar and salt</p><p>Heat the oil, fry the cumin and chilli for 30 seconds and add the potatoes</p><p>Add the tapioca and cook over medium heat for 5–7 minutes until the pearls turn translucent, stirring gently</p><p>Finish with lime juice and coriander</p>",
